WEBVTT

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:02.680
Right now, I've got four coding agents

00:00:02.680 --> 00:00:04.230
running across five projects.

00:00:04.580 --> 00:00:05.760
One of them has been waiting on me

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:08.280
for 20 minutes and I have no idea which

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:09.080
one.

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:11.590
I'm Nic and that's why I built Styx.

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:13.610
If you run Claude Code,

00:00:14.320 --> 00:00:15.900
Codex, Gemini or Cursor on more than

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:17.550
one project, you know the feeling.

00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:20.020
Every agent lives in its own terminal

00:00:20.020 --> 00:00:22.300
on its own branch in some window you're

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:24.380
not looking at. And every tool that

00:00:24.380 --> 00:00:26.380
promises to fix it wants you to move

00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:28.910
in a new editor, a new workspace,

00:00:29.200 --> 00:00:30.510
one project at a time.

00:00:31.140 --> 00:00:32.290
Then there's access.

00:00:32.620 --> 00:00:34.460
The useful agents need to touch real

00:00:34.460 --> 00:00:36.010
things like your deploys,

00:00:36.060 --> 00:00:37.470
your database, your servers.

00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:39.560
So you either paste in a token and

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:41.790
hope or you sit there and watch it.

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:44.590
I've done both and I didn't love either.

00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:47.350
Styx fixes that in three ways.

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:49.610
First, everything's in one window.

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:51.470
Every project, every agent.

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:53.440
You can see what's waiting on you and

00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:55.430
one keystroke takes you straight there.

00:00:55.900 --> 00:00:56.700
Second,

00:00:57.120 --> 00:00:58.390
it doesn't replace anything.

00:00:58.720 --> 00:01:00.600
It sits on top of the editor you already

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:02.820
use and runs on the Claude and Codex

00:01:02.820 --> 00:01:04.690
subscriptions you already pay for.

00:01:05.380 --> 00:01:07.050
It picks up your recent folders,

00:01:07.420 --> 00:01:09.780
key bindings and theme and one key

00:01:09.780 --> 00:01:11.730
opens anything back in your editor.

00:01:12.760 --> 00:01:13.560
Third,

00:01:13.600 --> 00:01:15.960
it holds your keys so your agents don't

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:16.760
have to.

00:01:16.960 --> 00:01:18.410
When an agent wants production,

00:01:18.480 --> 00:01:20.960
it stops and asks and you approve it

00:01:20.960 --> 00:01:22.510
for a set window of time.

00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:25.140
Every request and every approval goes

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:26.970
into a log nobody can edit,

00:01:27.120 --> 00:01:28.690
not the agents and not me.

00:01:29.460 --> 00:01:31.390
Every project, every agent,

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:33.130
every key in one window.

00:01:33.680 --> 00:01:35.580
It's free right now and it's on Mac

00:01:35.580 --> 00:01:36.380
today.
